Key change: `Principal = "*"` (any AWS principal, unauthenticated) was replaced with a scoped `Principal` referencing the bucket owner's account ARN via `data.aws_caller_identity.current`, satisfying CKV_AWS_70. I also added `aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block` as defense-in-depth so the bucket can't be made public even if the policy changes later. If a different, specific principal (e.g., another account, an IAM role, or a CloudFront OAI) should have access instead, swap the `AWS` ARN accordingly — the important part is that it is never `"*"`.
